<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pihhuniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pihhuniya was a Kaska leader of the late 14th century BCE, known from the annals of the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-ii">Mursili II</a>. The annals say that, unlike other Kaska chiefs, he ruled 'in the manner of a king' and raided Hittite lands as far as the Upper Land. Mursili II defeated him and took him prisoner to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a>.</p></div>
